10. Impact can no longer be a fixed animation key

The current clip emits its attack event at a fixed impact frame. That only works because the current trajectory is fixed.

With dynamic trajectories:

launch can remain a phase event;
spear_commit can remain a phase event;
audio and visual whoosh cues can remain authored;
actual impact must come from simulation collision or terrain contact.

The simulation already owns gameplay truth and consumes animation tags; GEOM.POSE explicitly does not process events or choose clips.

On actual contact, the choreography player branches:

terrain contact  -> ground_stick
creature contact -> air_hit
no contact       -> miss_recover

This prevents an airborne Zixxtrixx from playing a ground-impact event in empty sky merely because clip key 56 arrived.

11. Recovery also becomes programmable

The current fixed recovery tries to:

extract;
finish another turn;
restore the S;
return the root;
close the loop;

within a very short tail section of the monolithic clip.

Replace it with explicit branches.

Ground recovery
Remain embedded.
Small biological bow and impact wave.
Pull out along the spear axis.
Confirm the tip is clear.
Reform the S head-to-tail.
Settle onto the terrain.
Air recovery
Recoil from the hit.
Spear shape loosens.
Head and neck regain curvature first.
The S travels down the body.
Transition into controlled fall, flight or landing.
Miss recovery
Continue past the target.
Bend out of the spear while retaining momentum.
Transition into fall or turn-around.

The same recover_to_s deformation can be shared, but its root trajectory and endpoint are plan-dependent.

